<h2>Overview</h2>
<p>Hlabeard Productions, in collaboration with the SATO48 Film Challenge, presents "FiveFest"—a dynamic festival dedicated to celebrating the art of short films with a maximum length of five minutes.</p>

<h2>Submission Guidelines</h2>
<h3>1. Film Duration and Content</h3>
<p>Films must be exactly 5 minutes or less in length including credits. You are not allowed to upload a file that is longer than 5 minutes in duration.</p>
<p>Non-English dialogue films must include English subtitles or be dubbed in English.</p>
<p>Do not upload works in progress. Uploaded films must be complete and theater-projection ready.</p>
<p>The film's genre must be one of the following: Animation, Comedy, Documentary, Drama, Experimental, Horror, Music Video, Musical.</p>
<h3>2. Technical Requirements</h3>
<p>The minimum resolution is 720p.</p>
<p>Submitted films must have clear audio quality.</p>
<p>A film Poster and any other Promotional Materials are encouraged (though not required) to be uploaded.</p>
<h3>3. Eligibility</h3>
<p>Open to all filmmakers, regardless of age, region, production date of film, or content within specified genres.</p>
<h3>4. Submission Process</h3>
<p>FilmFreeway.</p>

<h2>Judging and Awards</h2>
<h3>5. Judging Panel</h3>
<p>A select group of industry professionals and esteemed members of the filmmaking community will judge the entries.</p>
<p>Registered team members from last year's SATO48-Challenge are automatically opted IN and therefore may participate as Academy Judges if they so elect.</p>
<h3>6. Prizes</h3>
<ul>
<li>Best Animation</li>
<li>Best Comedy</li>
<li>Best Documentary</li>
<li>Best Drama</li>
<li>Best Experimental Film</li>
<li>Best Horror</li>
<li>Best Music Video</li>
<li>Best Musical</li>
</ul>

<h2>Venue and Event Details</h2>
<h3>7. Festival Locations (depending on needed capacity)</h3>
<p>Alamo Drafthouse Cinema, Springfield, Missouri (The largest Alamo Drafthouse Cinema in the United States)</p>
<h3>8. FiveFest Programming</h3>
<p>All films are accepted into FiveFest, as follows:</p>
<p>Accepted films will receive a FiveFest Scorecard detailing, in the aggregate, how the Academy Judges responded to their film and an exclusive month-long online screening.</p>
<p>Some films will be selected for (a) an in-theater screening at a Festival Location, and (b) acknowledged as a Nominee at October FiveFest Awards Ceremony.</p>
<p>The winning film in each genre — for whom a representative of the film is present and checked in at the October FiveFest Awards Ceremony — receives the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>Statuette</li>
<li>On-stage acceptance speech opportunity</li>
<li>Backstage interview</li>
</ul>
<h3>9. Notification of Your Acceptance Level</h3>
<p>You are notified via email of your film's Acceptance Level.</p>
<h3>10. FiveFest Dates To Save</h3>
<p>The submission closing date - September 1, 2026</p>
<p>In-theater screening, if applicable to your film, takes place at a date/time to be determined by capacity of Festival Locations.</p>
<p>October FiveFest Awards Ceremony - Exact Date TBD, 2nd Week of October</p>
<p>Online viewing, applicable to all films, takes place - TBD</p>

<h2>Legal Terms and Conditions</h2>
<h3>11. Film Rights</h3>
<p>Entrant must own all rights to their film and its content.</p>
<p>All Entrants grant Hlabeard Productions and SATO48 the following:</p>
<p>In-theater screening and paywall online usage rights for the duration of SATO48-2024 FiveFest.</p>
<p>Free online usage rights within Festival Manager and promotional usage rights in perpetuity.</p>
<p>Entrant holds Hlabeard Productions, SATO48, and all other parties connected to SATO48, harmless in all respects.</p>
<h3>12. Endorsement</h3>
<p>Participation in FiveFest by Entrant is not an endorsement by Hlabeard Productions, nor SATO48, of the film's content.</p>
<h3>13. Liability</h3>
<p>Hlabeard Productions and SATO48 are not liable for any losses or damages incurred for any reason by Entrant.</p>
<h3>14. Cancellation &amp; Delays</h3>
<p>In case of unavoidable cancellations or delays, efforts will be made to reschedule. No liability by Hlabeard Productions nor SATO48 is assumed for losses incurred due to such cancellations.</p>

<h2>Accessibility and Inclusion</h2>
<h3>15. Accessibility</h3>
<p>FiveFest venues are wheelchair accessible.</p>
<h3>16. Inclusion</h3>
<p>FiveFest is committed to diversity and inclusion.</p>

<h2>Contact Information</h2>
<h3>17. Inquiry Handling</h3>
<p>All inquiries should be sent to:</p>
<p><a href="mailto:support@sato48.com">support@sato48.com</a></p>
<p>or at:</p>
<p><a href="https://help.sato48.com/en/">https://help.sato48.com</a></p>
<p>END</p>

<h2 id="genre-criteria">Appendix: Prize Criteria by Genre</h2>
<h3>Animation</h3>
<ol><li>Innovation and Creativity in Animation Techniques</li><li>Storytelling Quality and Emotional Impact</li><li>Artistic Merit and Design</li><li>Voice Acting Performances</li><li>Enhancement of Animation as an Art Form</li></ol>
<h3>Comedy</h3>
<ol><li>Originality and Quality of the Script</li><li>Timing and Delivery of Comedic Elements</li><li>Overall Contribution to the Genre of Comedy</li><li>Ensemble Cast Performance and Chemistry</li><li>Direction that Brings Out the Humor in the Film</li></ol>
<h3>Documentary</h3>
<ul><li>Subject Matter Depth and Research Quality</li><li>Narrative Structure and Pacing</li><li>Cinematography and Visual Cohesion</li><li>Impact and Relevance</li><li>Originality and Insight</li></ul>
<h3>Drama</h3>
<ol><li>Depth and Complexity of Characters and Storyline</li><li>Quality of Performances by the Actors</li><li>Direction and Pacing of the Narrative</li><li>Cinematic Craftsmanship</li><li>Overall Impact on the Drama Genre</li></ol>
<h3>Experimental Film</h3>
<ul><li>Innovation in Film Techniques</li><li>Narrative and Conceptual Ambiguity</li><li>Visual and Aural Design</li><li>Engagement and Provocation</li><li>Innovative Impact</li></ul>
<h3>Horror</h3>
<ol><li>Ability to Elicit Fear, Suspense, and Thrill</li><li>Originality of the Concept and Execution</li><li>Technical Prowess in Creating a Horror Atmosphere</li><li>Quality and Depth of the Storyline</li><li>Influence on the Horror Genre and Overall Quality</li></ol>
<h3>Music Video</h3>
<ul><li>Creativity and Originality in Visual Presentation</li><li>Integration of Music with Visuals</li><li>Direction and Choreography</li><li>Technical Quality</li><li>Cultural or Artistic Impact</li></ul>
<h3>Musical</h3>
<ol><li>Integration of Music and Narrative</li><li>Quality of Musical Numbers</li><li>Choreography and Direction of Musical Sequences</li><li>Overall Contribution to the Genre of Musical Films</li><li>Direction that Highlights the Film's Musical Aspects</li></ol>

